{"message":"Thank you for confirming. I found no completed unauthorized transactions in the reviewed activity, but card ending in 5827 has suspicious failed ATM attempts in Tijuana while you were in Denver. I cannot unlock that card through chat; I recommend permanently closing it and issuing a replacement. Closing is irreversible—would you like me to proceed?

Card ending in 4518 has a security hold and you’re unsure whether the attempts were yours, so it requires review by our security team. Would you like me to transfer you for that card?

Cards ending in 3941 and 7263 had attempts you confirmed were yours. I can reset their PINs so they can be used again. To proceed, provide a separate new 4-digit PIN for each card. Each PIN must not be sequential, all the same digit, your birth year, or your birth month/day. Do not reuse a PIN you use elsewhere."}
